unts exact \u0928\u0939\u0940\u0902 (torch.profiler optional deep-check)\u0964\n\n## 10. Assumptions vs fixed task requirements\n\n**Fixed (source-verified):** /workspace = task.json only; design-only task; network \u092c\u0902\u0926 (empirically verified); Python 3.14.4; \u0915\u094b\u0908 torch/torchopt/numpy installed \u0928\u0939\u0940\u0902; CPU-only 224 cores; \u0915\u094b\u0908 dataset \u0928\u0939\u0940\u0902\u0964\n**Assumptions (source \u0915\u0941\u091b \u0928\u0939\u0940\u0902 \u0915\u0939\u0924\u093e):** TorchOpt API \u0915\u093e \u0905\u0938\u094d\u0924\u093f\u0924\u094d\u0935/\u0928\u093e\u092e/semantics (\u00a72); \"intermediate reuse\" \u0915\u0925\u094d\u092f \u0915\u093e \u0924\u093e\u0924\u094d\u092a\u0930\u094d\u092f\u094d\u092f A1/A2 \u092e\u0947\u0902 \u0938\u0947 \u0915\u094b\u0908; resource budget \u22642 CPU-hours; stability \u0915\u0940 \u00a75 \u092a\u0930\u093f\u092d\u093e\u0937\u093e; synthetic workloads \u092a\u0930\u094d\u092f\u093e\u092a\u094d\u0924\u0924\u093e; expected outcome \u00a77 D3 pattern (pure hypothesis); execution-variant \u0915\u093e version band (\u00a78)\u0964", "evidence": "Repository/environment observations underpinning the design: (1) /workspace contains only task.json (521 B) stating \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\" \u2014 no TorchOpt source exists to verify API names, hence Gate 0 and the A1-vs-A2 dual-interpretation retention. (2) import torch/torchopt \u2192 ModuleNotFoundError; pip list has no torch/numpy/scipy/jax; filesystem search (find / maxdepth 6, patterns *torch*) \u2192 zero hits; no wheel cache beyond pip/setuptools \u2192 execution infeasible here; \u00a79 written accordingly. (3) Network empirically blocked: socket to pypi.org:443 \u2192 gaierror DNS failure \u2192 \u00a78 requires offline pre-provisioned wheel index. (4) Platform: x86_64, glibc 2.43, kernel 7.0, AVX-512 flags incl. avx512_bf16/vnni, nproc=224, ~2 TB RAM \u2192 justifies thread-pinning/subprocess isola